WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:02.682
I start by creating a workflow file

00:02.682 --> 00:05.065
for this project. The first step checks

00:05.065 --> 00:07.447
out the code. I add Deslop immediately

00:07.447 --> 00:09.830
after it, so GitHub can check the

00:09.830 --> 00:12.212
files and produce a report whenever I

00:12.212 --> 00:13.233
run this workflow.

00:14.033 --> 00:16.377
Here I choose the released version of

00:16.377 --> 00:18.720
Deslop that this workflow will use. I

00:18.720 --> 00:21.064
keep the version written in the file,

00:21.064 --> 00:23.407
so another release cannot silently change the

00:23.407 --> 00:25.751
check. The settings are saved alongside the

00:25.751 --> 00:27.090
rest of the project.

00:27.890 --> 00:29.996
For the first run, I ask for

00:29.996 --> 00:32.102
a report without blocking the build. Once

00:32.102 --> 00:34.209
I have reviewed the result, I can

00:34.209 --> 00:36.315
set a limit. Here I use five

00:36.315 --> 00:38.421
percent as an example, then run the

00:38.421 --> 00:40.527
same check locally and inspect why it

00:40.527 --> 00:40.828
fails.

00:41.628 --> 00:43.784
For a check on new code, I

00:43.784 --> 00:45.939
save my changes to a file and

00:45.939 --> 00:48.095
select only the added lines. Deslop still

00:48.095 --> 00:50.251
looks through the project for matching copies.

00:50.251 --> 00:52.407
I read the result to see which

00:52.407 --> 00:54.563
new code caused the check to fail.
